  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#AnnotationProperty" ]
}, {
  "@id" : "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty" ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://ref.gs1.org/cbv/BTT",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://ref.gs1.org/cbv/BizStep",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://ref.gs1.org/cbv/Disp",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://ref.gs1.org/cbv/SDT",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/AggregationEvent",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "The event type AggregationEvent describes events that apply to objects that have been aggregated to one another. In such an event, there is a set of 'contained' objects that have been aggregated within a 'containing' entity that's meant to identify the aggregation itself.  This event type is intended to be used for 'aggregations', meaning an association where there is a strong physical relationship between the containing and the contained objects such that they will all occupy the same location at the same time, until such time as they are disaggregated."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@value" : "AggregationEvent"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/EPCISEvent"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2003/06/sw-vocab-status/ns#term_status" : [ {
    "@value" : "stable"
  } ],
  "https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/jsonldUriLabel" : [ {
    "@value" : "eventID"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/AssociationEvent",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "The event type AssociationEvent describes the association or disassociation of one or several physical objects with a parent object or a specific physical location.  Like the AggregationEvent, the AssociationEvent is also used to capture associations where there is a strong physical relationship between the containing and the contained objects such that they will all occupy the same location at the same time, until such time as they are disaggregated. However, the AggregationEvent does not allow for associations of objects with physical locations;  if action is DELETE while omitting the childEPC and childQuantityList field, all contained children are disaggregated from the containing parent. Because there are situations in which associations are more permanent, i.e. beyond the physical flow of goods (e.g. packing/unpacking and loading/unloading), an AssociationEvent SHOULD be used: (a) when objects need to be associated with a physical location or (b) when the parent object could also be subject to other, more temporary associations (i.e. captured using AggregationEvent)."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@value" : "AssociationEvent"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/EPCISEvent"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2003/06/sw-vocab-status/ns#term_status" : [ {
    "@value" : "stable"
  } ],
  "https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/jsonldUriLabel" : [ {
    "@value" : "eventID"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/BizTransaction",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Document that describes a particular business transaction. An example is a specific Purchase Order or Despatch Advice. Business Transaction information may be included in EPCIS events to record an event's participation in particular business transactions."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@value" : "BizTransaction"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2003/06/sw-vocab-status/ns#term_status" : [ {
    "@value" : "stable"
  } ],
  "https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/jsonldUriLabel" : [ {
    "@value" : "bizTransaction"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/EPCISEvent",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "A logistics event. This is a common superclass (base type) for all EPCIS events. All of the more specific event types are subclasses of EPCISEvent."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@value" : "EPCISEvent"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#disjointWith" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://w3id.org/eudpp#DPPEventRecord"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2003/06/sw-vocab-status/ns#term_status" : [ {
    "@value" : "stable"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/ObjectEvent",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "An ObjectEvent captures information about an event pertaining to one or more physical or digital objects identified by instance-level (EPC) or class-level (EPC Class) identifiers. In most situations, an ObjectEvent is envisioned to represent an actual observations of objects, but strictly speaking it can be used for any event a Capturing Application wants to assert about objects, including for example capturing the fact that an expected observation failed to occur."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@value" : "ObjectEvent"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/EPCISEvent"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2003/06/sw-vocab-status/ns#term_status" : [ {
    "@value" : "stable"
  } ],
  "https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/jsonldUriLabel" : [ {
    "@value" : "eventID"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/QuantityElement",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "A QuantityElement is a structure that identifies objects identified by a specific class-level identifier, either a specific quantity or an unspecified quantity."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@value" : "QuantityElement"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2003/06/sw-vocab-status/ns#term_status" : [ {
    "@value" : "stable"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/SensorReport",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/SourceOrDestination",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Provides additional business context when an EPCIS event is part of a business transfer; that is, a process in which there is a change of location, or transfer of ownership, or transfer of possession of physical or digital objects. Within a specified type of transfer, the business transfer is from the Source to the Destination."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@value" : "Source or Destination"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2003/06/sw-vocab-status/ns#term_status" : [ {
    "@value" : "stable"
  } ],
  "https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/jsonldUriLabel" : [ {
    "@value" : "id"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/TransactionEvent",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "The event type TransactionEvent describes the association or disassociation of physical or digital objects to one or more business transactions. While other event types have an optional bizTransactionList field that may be used to provide context for an event, the TransactionEvent is used to declare in an unequivocal way that certain objects have been associated or disassociated with one or more business transactions as part of the event."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@value" : "TransactionEvent"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/EPCISEvent"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2003/06/sw-vocab-status/ns#term_status" : [ {
    "@value" : "stable"
  } ],
  "https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/jsonldUriLabel" : [ {
    "@value" : "eventID"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/Transformation",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "A transformation business processes that takes a longer period of time than a single TransformationEvent, so is associated with a series of such events.\r\nWhen events share the same Transformation, the meaning is that the inputs to any of those events may have contributed in some way to each of the outputs in any of those same events."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@value" : "Transformation"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2003/06/sw-vocab-status/ns#term_status" : [ {
    "@value" : "stable"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/TransformationEvent",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "A TransformationEvent captures information about an event in which one or more physical or digital objects identified by instance-level (EPC) or class-level (EPC Class) identifiers are fully or partially consumed as inputs and one or more objects identified by instance-level (EPC) or class-level (EPC Class) identifiers are produced as outputs. The TransformationEvent captures the relationship between the inputs and the outputs, such that any of the inputs may have contributed in some way to each of the outputs."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@value" : "TransformationEvent"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/EPCISEvent"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2003/06/sw-vocab-status/ns#term_status" : [ {
    "@value" : "stable"
  } ],
  "https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/jsonldUriLabel" : [ {
    "@value" : "eventID"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/action",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty" ],
  "http://schema.org/domainIncludes" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/AggregationEvent"
  }, {
    "@id" : "https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/AssociationEvent"
  }, {
    "@id" : "https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/ObjectEvent"
  }, {
    "@id" : "https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/TransactionEvent"
  } ],
  "http://schema.org/rangeIncludes" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "How this event relates to the lifecycle of the EPCs named in this event."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain" : [ {
    "@id" : "_:genid20"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@value" : "action"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2003/06/sw-vocab-status/ns#term_status" : [ {
    "@value" : "stable"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/bizLocation",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty" ],
  "http://schema.org/domainIncludes" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/EPCISEvent"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "(Optional) The business location where the objects associated with the EPCs may be found, until contradicted by a subsequent event."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/EPCISEvent"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@value" : "bizLocation"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2003/06/sw-vocab-status/ns#term_status" : [ {
    "@value" : "stable"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/bizStep",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty" ],
  "http://schema.org/domainIncludes" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/EPCISEvent"
  } ],
  "http://schema.org/rangeIncludes" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://ref.gs1.org/cbv/BizStep"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "(Optional) The business step of which this event was a part."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/EPCISEvent"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@value" : "bizStep"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://ref.gs1.org/cbv/BizStep"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2003/06/sw-vocab-status/ns#term_status" : [ {
    "@value" : "stable"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/bizTransactionList",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty" ],
  "http://schema.org/domainIncludes" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/EPCISEvent"
  } ],
  "http://schema.org/rangeIncludes" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/BizTransaction"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "(Optional) An unordered list of business transactions that define the context of this event."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/EPCISEvent"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@value" : "bizTransactionList"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/BizTransaction"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2003/06/sw-vocab-status/ns#term_status" : [ {
    "@value" : "stable"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/bizTransactionType",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty" ],
  "http://schema.org/domainIncludes" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/BizTransaction"
  } ],
  "http://schema.org/rangeIncludes" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://ref.gs1.org/cbv/BTT"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "An identifier that indicates the type of BizTransaction document (e.g. Purchase Order, Despatch Advice)."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/BizTransaction"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@value" : "bizTransactionType"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://ref.gs1.org/cbv/BTT"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2003/06/sw-vocab-status/ns#term_status" : [ {
    "@value" : "stable"
  } ],
  "https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/jsonldLabel" : [ {
    "@value" : "type"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/childEPCs",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty" ],
  "http://schema.org/domainIncludes" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/AggregationEvent"
  }, {
    "@id" : "https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/AssociationEvent"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "(Optional) An unordered list of the EPCs of contained objects identified by instance-level identifiers. An AggregationEvent SHALL contain either a nonempty childEPCs, a non-empty childQuantityList, or both, except that both childEPCs and childQuantityList MAY be empty if action is DELETE, indicating that all children are disaggregated from the parent.  An AssociationEvent SHALL contain either a non-empty childEPCs, a non-empty childQuantityList, or both, except that both childEPCs and childQuantityList MAY be empty if action is DELETE, indicating that all children are disassociated from the parent."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain" : [ {
    "@id" : "_:genid1"
  } ],
